(Efficacy of Dietary Spice Components in Modifying Chronic Pain: A 3-Week Randomised) Tj
T*
(Crossover Trial) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Abstract) Tj
T*
(Thirty adults with moderate chronic pain completed a randomised crossover study examining) Tj
T*
(dietary spice interventions. Participants consuming turmeric-based formulations reported) Tj
T*
(meaningful reductions in daily pain intensity compared to baseline periods. Statistical) Tj
T*
(testing confirmed the significance of these improvements. When comparing various dosing) Tj
T*
(levels of turmeric alone, as well as turmeric combined with pepper bioenhancer, both) Tj
T*
(showed comparable benefit, though the distinction between individual dose levels did not) Tj
T*
(reach statistical significance. Medication use for pain relief showed no between-group) Tj
T*
(differences. No serious adverse events were reported during the study period. These) Tj
T*
(results indicate that incorporating turmeric into daily intake demonstrates measurable) Tj
T*
(analgesic potential in this population. The bioenhancer properties of pepper did not) Tj
T*
(substantially amplify outcomes in this preliminary assessment. Future research with larger) Tj
T*
(samples and longer intervention windows may clarify optimal dosing and whether combining) Tj
T*
(multiple botanical agents provides added benefit.) Tj
ET
